=======================================================================
CREDIT CHAIN (Mochy -> ViviMusic -> Metrolist -> InnerTune/ViMusic)
=======================================================================

1. Mochy Music — realidkroo — GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/realidkroo/Mochy-Music
   The parity baseline for this port: v8.4.2 build#1271 (versionCode
   73), commit bde01cb4. Everything this desktop application
   re-implements — playback, queue semantics, the audio DSP platform,
   the lyrics engine, the module/skin system, the importer, the
   integrations and the design language — comes from Mochy Music.
   Mochy adds on top of its ancestors: TV mode + phone link, Android
   Auto, Stage native DSP + Audio Lab, exclusive/USB output, the
   module platform + skins, crossmix, the song editor, the
   Spotify/Apple/Tidal/CSV importers, Discord RPC, i18n, the in-app
   updater and the docs site.

2. ViviMusic — vivizzz007 — GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/vivizzz007/vivi-music
   Mochy Music is a June 2026 snapshot re-import of ViviMusic that has
   since diverged massively. From ViviMusic this lineage carries the
   app shell, the Compose UI scaffolding, the innertube module, the
   lyrics provider stack, last.fm support, uCrop flows and the NEW-UI
   design language.

3. Metrolist — Mostafa Alagamy (MetrolistGroup) — GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/mostafaalagamy/Metrolist
   ViviMusic's code-derived base; the direct source of the
   InnerTubeX streaming engine (com.github.MetrolistGroup.innertubex),
   the widget manager, the PO-token approach and the base framework.

4. InnerTune (z-huang) and ViMusic (vfsfitvnm) — GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/z-huang/InnerTune
   https://github.com/vfsfitvnm/ViMusic
   The deep ancestors of the whole lineage: the strings corpus, the
   Room schema lineage, the KuGou + LRCLIB provider pattern and the
   app skeleton.

Upstream evidence for this chain is preserved in the Android
repository (AGENTS.md credits, AboutSheet.kt license entries, the
initial snapshot commits and the leftover com.music.vivi artifacts)
and is summarized in docs/BLUEPRINT.pdf, chapter 2.3.

